These fixtures accompany the native ports of MimeKit's benchmarks at
a4a10817. MimeKit's MIT license is included in LICENSE.

Copied from the MimeKit checkout, preserving its bytes:
  startrek.eml       Benchmarks/TestData/messages/startrek.eml
  content-length.mbox UnitTests/TestData/mbox/content-length.mbox.txt
  lorem-ipsum.txt    UnitTests/TestData/text/lorem-ipsum.txt
  wikipedia.txt     UnitTests/TestData/encoders/wikipedia.txt
  wikipedia.qp      UnitTests/TestData/encoders/wikipedia.qp

header-stress.eml is the MessageHeaderStressTest verbatim string extracted
from the committed Benchmarks/MimeParserBenchmarks.cs at that revision,
with doubled quotes unescaped and source newlines normalized to LF.
No local modifications or release-comparison harnesses were imported.

The benchmarks reuse tests/data/encodings/photo.jpg unchanged; it also matches
MimeKit's UnitTests/TestData/images/girl.jpg byte-for-byte. The existing
tests/data/encodings/photo.b64, tests/data/encodings/photo.uu, and
tests/data/mbox/input/jwz.mbox (paths relative to the repository root)
are converted to CRLF in untimed setup; this produces the same bytes as
the corresponding MimeKit checkout fixtures, without checking in another
10 MB copy of JWZ's mailbox. The wikipedia and lorem-ipsum fixtures here
differ in content, not just line endings, from GMime's older test fixtures.

Synthetic address, Base64-validator, nesting, and From-line cases are
generated in C. Base64 validator payloads use a deterministic native PRNG,
not the .NET Random sequence; lengths, line layouts, and chunk sizes match.
The UTF-8 address parser cases and Latin-1 address validator cases retain
their upstream byte encodings. In particular, the validator's international
case is not valid UTF-8, and its Groups case lacks separating commas.

The Unix newline-filter cases really contain LF-only data: upstream's
LoremIpsumUnix setup accidentally used Unix2DosFilter a second time.
Filter stream cases use explicit 4096-byte buffers (1024 for From filters),
rather than relying on .NET MemoryStream.CopyTo's implementation.

The byte-preserving .gitattributes in this directory applies to these fixtures.
